a to Guangdong, and east-west from Shandong to Gansu (Huang 1992:78-80, figs. 9-10), and the existence of an established set of ritual vessel types (li pitchers, dou cups, ding tripods, etc.), which were to have a paramount religious importance throughout the early dynastic period." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 881, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 808})
